      "key": [
        "Phobos",
        "Grand Symphony",
        "Golden Symphony"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Remus: Phobos (the Grand Symphony)",
      "content": "Remus's attempt to defy fate: a music-based will that guided ascended Remurians and was meant to take control of Fortune itself. It was made from Remus's power and Sybilla's wisdom and life. Lacking a will of its own, it absorbed Remurians' biases and began serving their selfish and destructive wishes.\n\nBoethius was devoured by it and became its puppet. Its attempt to restart in the present brought the 4.6 events of Petrichor, ending when the Traveler and Scylla destroyed it using Remus's Requiem.",
